ours second: abdominal pain or fullness, anemia, autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, bleeding, cellular immunodeficiency\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) vs Multiple Myeloma with Hypercalcemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n  Favours second: anemia, constipation, frequent urination, hyperviscosity syndrome, infections\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) vs Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) with Normal Differential:\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n  Favours second: autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, cellular immunodeficiency, chronic lymphatic leukemia"}
